Launch the Agent Inspector UI in a browser.

The inspector serves an embedded single-page application and proxies the SPA's
HTTP/SSE calls to a Foundry agent running on localhost (default port 8088).
The agent itself is started separately, for example via 'azd ai agent run'.

SSE chunks streamed to the SPA are also mirrored to your terminal so you can
watch progress without focusing the browser.

Usage
  azd ai inspector launch [flags]

Flags
      --conversation-id string : Optional explicit conversation ID for the SPA. If omitted, the SPA mints a fresh UUID.
      --inspector-port int     : Port the Agent Inspector UI listens on (default: 8087) (default 8087)
      --port int               : Localhost port of the agent the inspector targets (default: 8088) (default 8088)
      --session-id string      : Optional explicit session ID for the SPA. If omitted, the SPA mints a fresh UUID.

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for launch
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Launch the inspector against a local agent on the default port (8088),
  serving the UI on the default port (8087).
    azd ai inspector launch

  Launch with custom ports.
    azd ai inspector launch --port 9000 --inspector-port 9001

  Seed an explicit session/conversation (otherwise the SPA mints fresh UUIDs).
    azd ai inspector launch --session-id <uuid> --conversation-id <uuid>
